---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout
  title="Depth-aware effects"
  description="Varve's local-first relative DepthMap workflow for non-destructive blur, depth masks, and localized adjustments."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <div class="feature-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Depth-aware effects
      </nav>

      <h1>Depth-aware effects</h1>
      <p class="feature-intro">
        Generate or import one reusable relative DepthMap, then turn its ranges into masks or focus
        blur without flattening the photograph or baking in a one-off pixel result.
      </p>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>One depth field, many effects</h2>
        <p>
          Varve stores depth as a continuous, normalized field rather than a subject mask. Near and
          far regions remain available to future effects, focus transitions are adjustable, and the
          document keeps the original image as the source of truth.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Local-first:</strong> the optional depth model is downloaded explicitly and runs through Varve's inference path.</li>
          <li><strong>Reusable:</strong> save a map once, then use it from Depth Blur or the existing Depth Mask surface; accepted maps remain usable without the model.</li>
          <li><strong>Non-destructive:</strong> masks keep a range recipe beside resolved coverage, while Depth Blur remains a separate effect referencing the same map.</li>
          <li><strong>Focus control:</strong> choose focal depth, transition range, blur strength, and inversion; sample a point from the depth preview.</li>
          <li><strong>Depth masks:</strong> sample near/far values, combine soft coverage with existing raster masks, then refine with the familiar Mask brush.</li>
          <li><strong>Adjustment targeting:</strong> keep an adjustment's scope (what it processes) separate from its source-bound depth mask (where it appears).</li>
          <li><strong>Inspectable:</strong> valid-only histograms, near/far legend, source identity, map status, and explicit unsupported-input states prevent silent guesses.</li>
          <li><strong>Stable rendering:</strong> saved documents render the effect from the stored map without requiring the model at display time; the preview and replay use the same depth-aware compositor.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Fix the failure modes users notice</h2>
        <p>
          A greyed-out depth control, a mask that disappears with its blur effect, and a depth preview
          that samples the wrong pixel are workflow failures—not reasons to hide the feature. Varve
          shows the source and map status, rejects unsupported scalar inputs, keeps map and mask
          ownership separate, preserves manual coverage corrections, and maps picks through the
          actual contained preview. Reflections, transparent materials, hair, wires, heavy occlusion,
          and unusual viewpoints can still need a manual matte.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Workflow notes</h2>
        <p>
          The source asset, model provenance, preprocessing version, normalization, validity, and
          resource schema travel with the DepthMap metadata. The supported offline import is
          self-describing <code>.vdepth.json</code>; generated maps are relative, not calibrated
          metres. Corrupt or unavailable maps fail soft: Varve preserves the source pixels and
          reports the recovery action instead of silently replacing a protective mask.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="feature-cta">
        <h2>Explore the workflow</h2>
        <a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/depth-blur')} class="btn-default">Read the Depth Blur guide</a>
        <a href={sitePath('/features/color-effects')} class="btn-secondary">See Color &amp; Effects</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .feature-page { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0; }
  .breadcrumb { font-size: 0.875rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .feature-page h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.5rem); font-family: var(--font-editorial); margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .feature-intro { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .feature-section { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .feature-section h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .feature-section p, .feature-section li { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; }
  .feature-section ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .feature-section li + li { margin-top: 0.75rem; }
  .feature-cta { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding-top: 2rem; }
  .feature-cta h2 { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .btn-secondary { margin-left: 0.75rem; }
</style>
